    Add transcript-only space bound for exact S(n) and GEN-SORT
    
    Record the independently reviewed space refinement of the budgeted DFS:
    represent the state by the comparison transcript and decide comparability by
    graph reachability, so a frame stores only one comparison and a loop cursor.
    Work space drops from O(n^3 log n) bits (matrix-per-frame) to O(n log^2 n)
    bits, with the same 2^{O(n log^2 n)} time and the same PSPACE/EXPSPACE classes.
    
    The same DFS with a read-only dense n x n comparability matrix on the input
    tape gives GEN-SORT in DSPACE(O(sqrt(N) log^2 N)) for N = Omega(n^2), a
    sublinear-space upper bound, with k clamped to O(n log n) and polynomial
    per-node time.
    
    Add scripts/transcript_dfs.py and tests/test_transcript_dfs.py (n <= 5
    regression; exhaustive agreement with the memoized oracle for n <= 4).
    
    Space upper bounds only: no tightness, class separation, or time improvement.

